    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Both tests (`coreSegmentForKnownRegion` \u2192 `STANDARD_METRO`, `functionalitySegmentForUnknownRegion` \u2192 `STANDARD_REGIONAL`) pass, and `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a derived, read-only `ownerSegment` field to the Owner response, formatted `<TIER>_<AREA>`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`util/OwnerSegment.java`** (new) \u2014 computes the segment: `TIER` = `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel >= 3` else `STANDARD`; `AREA` = `METRO` when the locality is a known region else `REGIONAL`. Yields one of `PREMIUM_METRO`, `PREMIUM_REGIONAL`, `STANDARD_METRO`, `STANDARD_REGIONAL`.\n\n2. **`util/LocalityResolver.java`** \u2014 added `isKnownRegion(String)`, true only for NSW/VIC/QLD (reusing the existing region table), so the \"known region\" test lives with the other locality logic.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the `ownerSegment` mapping expression (and the import), reusing the same derivations already used for `membershipLevel` (`MembershipLevel.levelOf(pointsOf(owner))`) and `locality` (`LocalityResolver.regionOfCustomerCode(...)`) so the segment stays consistent with those existing fields.\n\n4. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared `ownerSegment` on the Owner schema (read-only string with the spec's description/example), so the generated DTO carries the field.\n\nThis follows the repo's existing pattern for derived owner fields (a small `util` class exposed through a MapStruct `expression` mapping) rather than any controller code.",
